    "narrative": "For this slate, the optimal strategy for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on exploiting high-upside matchups against favorable arms. **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) represent our strongest plays today. **James Wood** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a slow opposing delivery that heavily favors our stolen base aggression, while **Mickey Moniak** is positioned perfectly in the #2 hole with a significant 14% platoon edge against Bradley. **Corbin Carroll** (74.38) remains an elite start despite the modest park penalty, as his matchup against the pitcher\u2019s expected ERA of 4.65 provides a robust cushion to produce counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup was keeping **Seiya Suzuki** on the bench. With a score of 45.43, he was the closest candidate to cracking the order, but the optimizer prioritized the high floor of **Brice Turang** and **Gabriel Moreno** given the difficulty of the matchup against a 2.74 xERA arm. We are monitoring **Jose Caballero** closely; while his 71.07 score is impressive due to his platoon advantage against Tolle, there is a 35% risk of rain that could shorten his day. Meanwhile, we continue to carry **Trevor Story** on the IL while awaiting his return, as our depth\u2014including **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Carson Williams**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014must maintain our offensive pressure in the interim. \n\nManagers should note that several slots remain subject to final lineup confirmation, particularly **Dalton Rushing** and **Max Muncy**. While both are currently slotted into the active roster, their late-order placement in pending lineups slightly suppresses their ceiling. Should the official lineups drop and show either **Dalton Rushing** or **Max Muncy** outside of the starting nine, they will be handled according to our standard efficiency protocol to protect our remaining game caps.",
